# DIAGNOSTICS

A short write is `io`; others are the server's errors, or the ring's (`transport(peerClosed)` when the file's server went, `wire(invalidValue)` when it answered what wasn't asked).

# BUGS

The ring's size is fixed: 16 entries of 128 KiB.
A write's failure is said late, at a later call; one whose caller neither calls again nor finishes is lost, as when a program exits mid-write.
FDIO waits for every file's writes at exit, so a tier-1 program's are done whether or not it closes them.
fs(4) doesn't serve `attach` yet, so its files stay on messages.
